# ================================================================================
WHAT THIS FORM DOES - STEP BY STEP

1. Convert Display Data
- Converts WBS POSID from external (PC.00000.1) to internal (PC000001)
- Populates gs_header with all field values
1. Save Request
- Calls go_builder->save_request
- Gets request number (e.g., ‘0000000001’)
- Status is saved as ‘DRAFT’ initially
1. Get Approvers
- Queries ZTB_A2R_CONFTAB2 for approver positions
- Queries HRP1001 to get VARYF values for each position
- Returns:
  - lv_appr1 = ‘30000’ (Position ID)
  - lt_l1_approvers = table of VARYF (‘USHQ75177’, ‘USEV92123’, etc.)
  - lv_auto = ‘X’ if no approvers found
1. Update Status to PENDING
- UPDATE ztb_a2r_wbshdr SET request_status = ‘PENDING’
- COMMIT WORK AND WAIT ← CRITICAL!
- This commits BEFORE workflow trigger
1. Trigger Workflow or Auto-Approve
- If lv_auto = ‘X’: Call create_project directly
- Else: Call trigger_workflow with ALL parameters
1. Show Success Message
- If workflow triggered: “Request submitted for approval”
- If auto-approved: “Request approved and project created”

# ================================================================================
EXPECTED BEHAVIOR AFTER FIX

When user clicks SUBMIT:

1. ✅ Screen shows: “Request 0000000001 submitted for approval”
1. ✅ Database shows:
   SELECT * FROM ztb_a2r_wbshdr WHERE zreq_num = ‘0000000001’
   → request_status = ‘PENDING’ (not ‘DRAFT’)
1. ✅ Workflow is created in SAP inbox
1. ✅ Approvers receive workflow item

If workflow trigger fails:

- ❌ Status stays ‘PENDING’ in database
- ❌ Error message shows: “Workflow trigger failed”

